	&lt;!-- Ark: development levels, body count, Dawn Vault and projects (managerArk) --&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_foodsupply_1"&gt;1 grub per bullet&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_foodsupply_1_desc"&gt;A desperate struggle for food. A bullet buys 1 grub.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_foodsupply_2"&gt;2 grub per bullet&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_foodsupply_2_desc"&gt;Enough grub for daily needs while harvests and hunts go well. A bullet buys 2 grub. Body count -1.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_foodsupply_3"&gt;3 grub per bullet&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_foodsupply_3_desc"&gt;Almost everyone eats every day, with some reserves. A bullet buys 3 grub. Body count -2.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_foodsupply_4"&gt;4 grub per bullet&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_foodsupply_4_desc"&gt;Nobody goes hungry; cooking and brewing are refined. A bullet buys 4 grub. Body count -3.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_culture_1"&gt;Campfire tales&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_culture_1_desc"&gt;Apart from the Chroniclers, only tales around the barrel fires.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_culture_2"&gt;Basic literacy&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_culture_2_desc"&gt;Most can read and write a little; maybe a place of worship, plays or exhibitions.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_culture_3"&gt;Schools&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_culture_3_desc"&gt;Writing is advanced and widespread; maybe an organized school.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_culture_4"&gt;Self-government&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_culture_4_desc"&gt;The ideals of the Ancients are known; maybe some form of voting or participatory rule.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_technology_1"&gt;Gearheads only&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_technology_1_desc"&gt;Only the Gearheads understand technology; most artifacts are puzzles.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_technology_2"&gt;Mills and stills&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_technology_2_desc"&gt;Basic technical knowledge: simple constructions like a mill or a still.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_technology_3"&gt;Workshops&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_technology_3_desc"&gt;Mechanical construction: workshops, new roads, machines like a printing press.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_technology_4"&gt;Steam engines&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_technology_4_desc"&gt;On the edge of a revolution: steam engines, heliographs, electric lights, breech-loading guns.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_warfare_1_desc"&gt;Only simple barricades: the Ark is defenseless against outside enemies.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_warfare_2_desc"&gt;Scrap palisades and watchtowers, maybe some patrols.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_warfare_3_desc"&gt;Probably an organized militia, maybe an armory.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_step_warfare_4_desc"&gt;A standing army; the Ark is defended by home-made cannons and flamethrowers.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_battle_level"&gt;Battle Level %d&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_battle_level_alert"&gt;Battle Level +1 when the Ark is on alert.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_foodsupply_1"&gt;Normal prices&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_foodsupply_1_desc"&gt;Production covers what most residents need. Prices are not changed.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_foodsupply_2"&gt;Prices x2&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_foodsupply_2_desc"&gt;Some goods are hard to find, power cuts are more frequent and the black market grows. Prices are doubled.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_foodsupply_3"&gt;Prices x3&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_foodsupply_3_desc"&gt;Empty shelves, hoarding and looting in the Deep, longer blackouts. Prices are tripled.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_foodsupply_4"&gt;Prices x4&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_foodsupply_4_desc"&gt;Desperate shortages, looting even in the Core, no power in parts of the Deep. Prices are four times higher, when there is anything to buy.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_culture_1"&gt;Theaters open&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_culture_1_desc"&gt;Books are scarce, but the enclave keeps a busy cultural life of plays, films and books.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_culture_2"&gt;Theaters closing&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_culture_2_desc"&gt;Censorship, threats and lack of resources close theaters; some cinemas show forbidden films in protest.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_culture_3"&gt;Propaganda&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_culture_3_desc"&gt;Conformity grows: what remains shows propaganda of the Houses, and illegal radio stations broadcast protests.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_culture_4"&gt;Cultural life stopped&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_culture_4_desc"&gt;Almost nothing is left but the Voice of Dawn and its endless propaganda.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_technology_1"&gt;Research goes on&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_technology_1_desc"&gt;The scholars of the Academy keep working to bring humanity back to the surface. Artifacts that need more Science than the enclave has can no longer be made.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_technology_2"&gt;Programs closing&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_technology_2_desc"&gt;Some research programs close for lack of resources and rivalries; parts of the Academy are empty. Artifacts that need more Science than the enclave has can no longer be made.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_technology_3"&gt;Only vital research&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_technology_3_desc"&gt;Only the most vital projects go on, with fewer people and resources. Artifacts that need more Science than the enclave has can no longer be made.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_technology_4"&gt;Academy empty&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_technology_4_desc"&gt;The Academy is almost empty; the last scientists try to save what knowledge they can. Artifacts that need more Science than the enclave has can no longer be made.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_warfare_1"&gt;Incidents: 3 dice&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_warfare_1_desc"&gt;Crime is common, but guards and Judicators keep law and order. A House rolls 3 dice for an incident handled by other Judicators.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_warfare_2"&gt;Incidents: 4 dice&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_warfare_2_desc"&gt;More robberies and protests; gangs of the Deep hold whole blocks and workers form vigilante groups. A House rolls 4 dice for an incident handled by other Judicators.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_warfare_3"&gt;Incidents: 5 dice&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_warfare_3_desc"&gt;Unrest reaches the Core, where gangs grow stronger; shops post guards at the door. A House rolls 5 dice for an incident handled by other Judicators.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_warfare_4"&gt;Incidents: 6 dice&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="enclave_step_warfare_4_desc"&gt;Riots and looting in the Core, guards and Judicators attacked in the streets, gangs rule the Deep. A House rolls 6 dice for an incident handled by other Judicators.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_desc_bodycount"&gt;Body count of the session&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_tag_bodycount"&gt;[%d dead] [Population %d -&gt; %d]&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_vault_notartifact"&gt;Only artifacts can be handed over to the Dawn Vault (%s is not one).&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_vault_store"&gt;The %s is handed over to the Dawn Vault.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_vault_store_char"&gt;%s hands over the %s to the Dawn Vault.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_vault_remove"&gt;The %s is taken out of the Dawn Vault.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_text_dev_missing"&gt;%s %d (the Ark has %d)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_artifact_comprehend"&gt;%s must roll Comprehend to use the %s: the Ark needs %s to understand it.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_project_alreadycompleted"&gt;The project %s is already completed.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_project_inprogress"&gt;The project %s is already in progress.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_project_needs"&gt;The project %s needs %s.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_project_start"&gt;The People start the project %s (%d work points).&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_project_start_requires"&gt;The People start the project %s (%d work points). It also requires: %s.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_work_nochar"&gt;Choose one of your characters to work on the project.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_title_work"&gt;Work on the project&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_work_who"&gt;Who works on %s?&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_work_noskill"&gt;%s has none of the skills of the project (%s).&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_work_skill"&gt;Which skill does %s use?&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_work_pool"&gt;%s works on %s with %s: roll the dice pool of the character sheet (gear dice can be added).&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_tag_work_noprogress"&gt;[%s: no progress]&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_tag_work_progress"&gt;[%s: -%d WP, %d left]&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_tag_work_completed"&gt;[%s: COMPLETED]&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_project_completed"&gt;The project %s is completed.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_msg_project_destroyed"&gt;The project %s is destroyed.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_menu_project_complete"&gt;Complete project&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_menu_project_destroy"&gt;Destroy project&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="ark_menu_vault_remove"&gt;Take out of the Dawn Vault&lt;/string&gt;

	&lt;!-- Types of Boss (managerBoss) --&gt;
	&lt;string name="boss_desc_despot"&gt;Obsessed with power and with showing it; lets others do the dirty work, sees enemies everywhere and crushes any sign of rebellion.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="boss_desc_commander"&gt;Drills the followers like soldiers and does not mind getting dirty hands now and then.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="boss_desc_agitator"&gt;Inspires the People with fiery speeches about a better future; the other Bosses see the Agitator as a threat.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="boss_desc_revolutionary"&gt;Wants to overthrow the Elder and build a fair order: no private property, no Bosses, decisions by consensus.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="boss_desc_kingpin"&gt;Treats the followers almost as slaves and pushes huge projects through with violence.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="boss_desc_bureaucrat"&gt;A neutral leader who rules by the old rules and orders of the Elder.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="boss_desc_cultleader"&gt;Worshipped as divine by a cult of fanatics; any doubt is punished, and the cult keeps to itself.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="boss_desc_collector"&gt;Obsessed with artifacts of the Old Age; never hands anything over to the Dawn Vault.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="boss_desc_worker"&gt;Works side by side with the followers; wants to build something new instead of plotting.&lt;/string&gt;

	&lt;!-- Character: roles, resources and the sheet (managerChar, managerInventory, windows) --&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_msg_role_already"&gt;%s already has the role %s.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_text_role_skill"&gt;skill %s&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_msg_role_taken"&gt;%s takes the role %s.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_msg_role_taken_gear"&gt;%s takes the role %s: %s.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_title_talent"&gt;Talent&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_msg_choose_talent"&gt;Choose the talent of your %s.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_title_weapon"&gt;Weapon&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_msg_choose_weapon"&gt;Choose the starting weapon of your %s.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_msg_talent_learned"&gt;%s learns the talent %s.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_msg_weapon_taken"&gt;%s takes the weapon %s.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="resource_grub"&gt;Grub&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="resource_water"&gt;Water&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="resource_bullets"&gt;Bullets&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="resource_booze"&gt;Booze&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="inventory_msg_starting"&gt;%s starts with %s. Roll them and add them to the resources in the Inventory tab.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_label_people"&gt;People&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_label_contacts"&gt;Contacts&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_tooltip_animaltype"&gt;Animal type of the character (Genlab Alpha)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_tooltip_animaltype_key"&gt;Key attribute: %s. Recovers Instinct: %s. Species: %s.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_desc_armor"&gt;{name} check:&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_desc_house_reroll"&gt;House %s: %d rerolled&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_msg_damage"&gt;%d damage.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="char_msg_weapon_damage"&gt;%s damage %s&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="npc_tooltip_rank_genlab"&gt;Rank of the NPC (Genlab Alpha): it changes the Dominate rolls between it and the characters&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="npc_tooltip_rank_elysium"&gt;Reputation of the NPC (Elysium): it changes the Manipulate rolls between it and the characters&lt;/string&gt;

	&lt;!-- Mutations, animal powers, contacts and implants (managerPowers) --&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_wild_1"&gt;The beast takes over: the GM plays you as an NPC, you flee into the wild and fight anyone who stops you. Someone can heal you after 1D6 hours; then you gain a new animal power of your choice&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_wild_2"&gt;You must flee from or fight someone of your choice, friend or foe, until one of you is broken; then you cannot speak or use tools&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_wild_3"&gt;You lose speech, the use of tools and the Comprehend skill for 1D6 days&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_wild_4"&gt;You can only make animal sounds for 1D6 days, but you can still use your skills&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_wild_5"&gt;Your human side suppresses the beast: you lose all your Wild Points, gain none and cannot use Dominate for 1D6 days&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_wild_6"&gt;Harmony with the beast: you get back the Wild Points spent and can use the power again at once&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_reaction_1"&gt;The contact feels used and refuses: you lose the contact, who becomes your enemy&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_reaction_2"&gt;The contact helps, but first wants a favor in return&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_reaction_3"&gt;The contact helps, but wants help with something hard later, and cannot be activated again until you do it&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_reaction_4"&gt;The contact helps, but wants D6 credits for the trouble&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_reaction_5"&gt;The contact helps, but also does something for their own benefit that may bring you trouble&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_reaction_6"&gt;The contact goes all in and convinces someone else to help you: you gain a new contact of your choice&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_msg_max_abilities"&gt;%s already has %d animal powers and mutations, the most an animal can have. A stained animal that gains a new mutation must remove another mutation first.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_msg_no_points"&gt;%s has no points to use powers.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_msg_not_enough"&gt;%s has %d %s and cannot spend %d.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_tag_wild"&gt;[WILD EFFECT]&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_desc_wild"&gt;Wild effect&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_msg_session_notgenlab"&gt;Only Genlab Alpha gives wild points at the start of the session.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_msg_session_gain"&gt;%s gains %d WP for the session (%d animal powers) [WP %d -&gt; %d]&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_msg_session_gm"&gt;The GM starts the session with %d wild points.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_text_gm_pool"&gt;GM WP +%d&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_msg_contact_noinfluence"&gt;Set the influence points to spend on the contact first.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_desc_contact"&gt;Contact: %s (%d %s)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_tag_negative_reaction"&gt;[NEGATIVE REACTION]&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_tag_contact_helps"&gt;[The contact helps]&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_desc_reaction"&gt;Negative reaction&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_msg_implant_nobonus"&gt;The implant has no bonus to use.&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_text_fever_1"&gt;MECHANICAL FEVER: tremors&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_text_fever_2"&gt;MECHANICAL FEVER: chills and spasms, Agility 0 (Fatigue) BROKEN&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="powers_text_psychosis"&gt;MECHANICAL PSYCHOSIS: attacks every living being at Near range until broken by damage, immune to other trauma; Empathy %d -&gt; %d for good&lt;/string&gt;

	&lt;!-- Rest and recovery (managerRecovery) --&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_condition_starving"&gt;hungry&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_condition_dehydrated"&gt;dehydrated&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_condition_sleepless"&gt;sleepless&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_condition_hypothermic"&gt;hypothermic&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_blocked"&gt;cannot recover %s while %s&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_no_loss"&gt;has no %s to recover&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_no_resource"&gt;has no %s left&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_recovers_points"&gt;recovers %d %s (%d %s)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_recovers"&gt;recovers %d %s&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_eat_condition"&gt;eats and is no longer hungry&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_drink_condition"&gt;drinks and is no longer dehydrated&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_sleep_condition"&gt;sleeps and is no longer sleepless&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_booze"&gt;drinks booze&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_booze_heals"&gt;, heals %s for 1D6 hours&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_text_and"&gt;and&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_option_eat_condition"&gt;Eat a ration of grub (no longer hungry)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_option_eat_points"&gt;Eat grub (1 ration per point of Strength)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_option_eat"&gt;Eat a ration of grub (recover Strength)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_option_drink_condition"&gt;Drink a ration of water (no longer dehydrated)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_option_drink_points"&gt;Drink water (1 ration per point of Agility)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_option_drink"&gt;Drink a ration of water (recover Agility)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_option_sleep_condition"&gt;Sleep four hours (no longer sleepless)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_option_sleep"&gt;Sleep four hours (recover Wits)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_option_share"&gt;%s (recover %s)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_option_booze"&gt;Drink a dose of booze (1 damage, 1 doubt)&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_title"&gt;Rest&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_msg_choose"&gt;%s rests at least four hours. Choose what to do:&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="recovery_msg_result"&gt;%s rests: %s.&lt;/string&gt;

	&lt;!-- Rot (managerRot) --&gt;
	&lt;string name="rot_level_0"&gt;Rot oasis: no rot points here&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="rot_level_1"&gt;Weak rot: 1 rot point per day&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="rot_level_2"&gt;Strong rot: 1 rot point per hour&lt;/string&gt;
	&lt;string name="rot_level_3"&gt;Rot hotspot: 1 rot point per minute&lt;/string&gt;
